      "content": "Stop the stinging immediately by applying a cool, wet compress, but avoid heavy oils or thick creams right now. Coconut oil or aloe vera might trap the heat, which is counterproductive when dealing with a fresh burn. For immediate relief, gently cool the area under cool running water for at least ten minutes to draw the heat out. If the redness is severe, you should consider applying a thin layer of an antibiotic ointment and monitoring it closely.",
